.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr den Befehl
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP NAME='CMPMSGF'.
Compare Message File (CMPMSGF) - Help
:P.
The Compare Message File (CMPMSGF) command compares two message
files. The result of the comparison is shown in a subfile.
:P.
Missing message descriptions can easily be put in sync by
pressing F9. Non-matching message descriptions can be flagged
as 'copy-to-left' or 'copy-to-right' to put them in sync.
:P.
Everything from the RTVM0400 format of the QMHRTVM API is
compared. In order to use the RTVM0400 format you should
be on V5R1 or above or apply one of the following PTFs:
:P.
:LINES.
   R450 - SF62999
   R430 - SF64296
   R440 - SF64297
:ELINES.
:P.
See APAR #SA89599 for additional information.
:P.
If you have to use the RTVM0300 format, then only the following
attributes are compared:
:P.
:UL.
:LI.Message severity
:LI.Alert index
:LI.Alert option
:LI.Log indicator
:LI.Message ID
:LI.Substitution Variables
:LI.Default Reply
:LI.CCSID conversion status indicator of text
:LI.CCSID conversion status indicator of replacement data
:LI.Coded character set identifier of text
:LI.Message
:LI.Message Help
:EUL.
:P.
Also the :HP2.CMPDATE:EHP2. and :HP2.CMPLVL:EHP2. parameter
does not work.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort NEWMSGF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/NEWMSGF   '.
New message file - Help
:XH3.New message file (NEWMSGF)
:P.
Specifies the name and library of the new-message file.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.message-file-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the new-message file.
.*
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched until the first
match is found.
.*
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the new-message
file.  If no library is specified as the current library for the
job, QGPL is used.
.*
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the library where the new-message file is located.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort OLDMSGF
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/OLDMSGF   '.
Old message file - Help
:XH3.Old message file (OLDMSGF)
:P.
Specifies the name and library of the old-message file.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.message-file-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the old-message file.
.*
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched until the first
match is found.
.*
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the old-message
file.  If no library is specified as the current library for the
job, QGPL is used.
.*
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the library where the old-message file is located.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort RANGE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/RANGE     '.
Range of message identifiers - Help
:XH3.Range of message identifiers (RANGE)
:P.
Specifies the range of message identifiers in the specified message files
for which message descriptions are compared.  All message
descriptions in the message files specified on the Message file prompt
(NEWMSGF/OLDMSGF parameter) can be compared by specifying *ALL on this
parameter.
:P.
If the starting message identifier is not specified, the message
descriptions begin with the first message in the specified message file.
If the ending message identifier is not specified, the default value,
*LAST, is used.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:XH3.Starting Message Identifier
:P.
The first of the two values in this parameter, called the startingen-ID
message identifier, specifies the message identifier of the first
message description to compare.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first message in the file specified on the Message file prompt
(NEWMSGF/OLDMSGF parameter) is the first message whose description is
compared.
:PT.:PV.lower-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the first message description
to be compared.
:EPARML.
:P.
:XH3.Ending Message Identifier
:P.
The second of the two values, called the ending message identifier,
specifies the message identifier for the last message description to be
compared.
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ONLY:EPK.
:PD.Only the message identifier specified as a starting message
identifier has its description compared.
:PT.:PV.*LAST:EPV.
:PD.The last message in the files is the last message whose description
is compared.
:PT.:PV.upper-value:EPV.
:PD.Specify the 7-character identifier of the last message description
to be compared.
:EPARML.
:P.
:XH3.Other Single Values:
:P.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.*ALL:EPV.
:PD.All message descriptions in the message files specified are
compared.  This value can only be specified in the first element
of this parameter.
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort CMPDATE
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/CMPDATE   '.
Compare modif./creation date - Help
:XH3.Compare modif./creation date (CMPDATE)
:P.
Specify *YES if the creation and modification dates should be
compared.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
.*
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Also the message creation and modification dates are compared.
.*
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The message creation and modification date are not compared.
.*
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort CMPLVL
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/CMPLVL    '.
Compare modif./creation level - Help
:XH3.Compare modif./creation level (CMPLVL)
:P.
Specify *YES if the creation and modification levels should be
compared.
:P.
:HP2.Attention::EHP2. *YES may not work properly, when the messages are changed
multiple times over a day.
:P.
Example:
:P.
Message #1 and message #2 are created at the same day. Message #1
was changed 2 times and message #2 was changed 3 times. However
the latest change was applied to message #1. So actually message #2
should be replaced by message #2. But since message #2 was changed
one times more than message #1, CMPMSGF suggest to replace message #1
by message #2.
:P.
:LINES.
   message #1 (2 changes)  <==  message #2 (3 changed)
:ELINES.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
.*
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Also the message creation and modification levels are compared.
.*
:PT.:PV.*NO:EPV.
:PD.The message creation and modification levels are not compared.
.*
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
.* Hilfetext fr Schlsselwort ERROR
.*--------------------------------------------------------------------
:HELP name='CMPMSGF/ERROR     '.
Show errors only - Help
:XH3.Show errors only (ERROR)
:P.
Specify *YES to show only non-matching message descriptions.
.*
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
.*
:PARML.
.*
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.All message descriptions are shown.
.*
:PT.:PV.*YES:EPV.
:PD.Only non-matching message descriptions are shown.
.*
:EPARML.
.*
:EHELP.
.*
